    <string name="import_help">Moving from another app</string>
    <string name="import_help_sub">Where to find the export in popular apps</string>
    <string name="import_help_text">Simplenote — on the web or desktop: Settings → Tools → Export notes. Pick the .zip you get.\n\nGoogle Keep — takeout.google.com, select only Keep and export. Pick the .zip or the .json files from it.\n\nEvernote — select notes, then Export → ENEX. Pick the .enex file.\n\nStandard Notes — Preferences → Backups → download a decrypted backup. Pick the .zip or the file inside it.\n\nObsidian, Joplin, Bear, Markor, Notion and others — export as Markdown or text, then pick the files or a .zip with them.\n\nYou can pick several files at once. Notes that are already in Cotes are skipped, tags become #tags at the end of a note, and notes from the trash are left out.</string>
